tt-local-generator (0.63.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * feat(create): the Create surface is now a resizable split, like browse mode.
    The form lives on the LEFT and expands to fill up to the divider — no more
    880px/1440px caps that floated the result pane in dead space on a wide
    window — and the result is a DETAIL PANE docked on the RIGHT (default ~440px,
    subtle left border). The divider is a draggable Gtk.Paned handle, so you can
    widen the result over the form or give the form the whole width. Because the
    result is a fixed side pane rather than a FlowBox cell whose natural width
    steered the layout, it can no longer wrap below the form or jitter as its
    text changes, so the old MaxWidthBin/prompt-width workarounds are obsolete
    (removed `_build_panes`/`_TWO_PANE_MAX_WIDTH`).

